# Server-side redirects for hosts that read this file (Netlify, Cloudflare
# Pages). They run BEFORE the HTML, so the browser never paints an interstitial
# and search engines see a real 301. The matching .html pages stay as the
# fallback for hosts that ignore this file (Render, GitHub Pages).
#
# Query strings are forwarded automatically, but the destination needs them
# RESHAPED (id -> doc, plus a tab), which a splat cannot express — so the
# query-string paths keep their HTML redirectors and only the path-shaped
# routes are handled here.

/persons/*        https://www.over.org.il/projects/ocoi?tab=graph&type=person&id=:splat        301
/companies/*      https://www.over.org.il/projects/ocoi?tab=graph&type=company&id=:splat       301
/associations/*   https://www.over.org.il/projects/ocoi?tab=graph&type=association&id=:splat   301
/domains/*        https://www.over.org.il/projects/ocoi?tab=graph&type=domain&id=:splat        301
/documents        https://www.over.org.il/projects/ocoi?tab=documents                          301

# The old API. Nothing here can serve it, and a silent 404 would look like an
# outage rather than a move — send callers to the documented replacement.
/api/v1/*         https://www.over.org.il/api/ocoi/:splat                                       301
